eading\\">\\n        <div class=\\"container\\">\\n            <div class=\\"row\\">\\n                <div class=\\"col-md-8 col-sm-8\\">\\n                    <h1>Guest Lecture</h1>\\n                </div>\\n                                <div class=\\"pathway col-md-4 col-sm-4 hidden-xs text-right\\">\\n                     <div id=\\"crumbs\\"><a href=\\"https://ucp.edu.pk\\">Home</a> &raquo; <a href=\\"https://ucp.edu.pk/./news/\\">News</a> &raquo; <span class=\\"current\\">Guest Lecture</span></div>                </div>\\n                            </div><!--/row-->\\n        </div><!--/container-->\\n    </div><!--/page-heading-->\\n\\n<div class=\\"top-sidebar\\">\\n    <div class=\\"container\\">\\n        <div class=\\"row\\">\\n                    </div><!--/row-->\\n    </div><!--/container-->\\n</div><!--/Top sidebar-->\\t<div id=\\"bsf_rt_marker\\"></div><p>Ms. Mirrat Gul, a senior Clinical Psychologist, was invited as a guest speaker in University of Central Punjab to deliver a lecture on Cognitive Behavior Therapy for patients of Depression and Anxiety to the students of M.S Clinical Psychology.<br >\\nCognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) is a form of psychotherapy that encourages patients to explore the relationship between their thoughts, feelings, and behaviors. This kind of treatment helps individuals in recovery, understand their self-destructive behavior, and work to modify their way of thinking. Cognitive Behavior Therapy is used for a variety of mental and Behavioral health disorders and is commonly used by therapist to treat anxiety and depression.<br >\\n&nbsp;<br >\\n\\n\\t\\t<style type=\\"text/css\\">\\n\\t\\t\\t#gallery-2 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmargin: auto;\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t#gallery-2 .gallery-item {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfloat: left;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmargin-top: 10px;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\ttext-align: center;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\twidth: 20%;\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t#gallery-2 img {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tborder: 2px solid #cfcfcf;\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t#gallery-2 .