89ec-57064c6b35be: url(\'https:\\\\/\\\\/ucp.edu.pk\\\\/wp-content\\\\/plugins\\\\/js_composer\\\\/assets\\\\/images\\\\/icons\\\\/balloon.png\');}\\",\\"hash\\":\\"3c01fdb8-87b6-4949-89ec-57064c6b35be\\",\\"url\\":\\"https:\\\\/\\\\/ucp.edu.pk\\\\/wp-content\\\\/plugins\\\\/js_composer\\\\/assets\\\\/images\\\\/icons\\\\/balloon.png\\"},{\\"selector\\":\\".vc_pixel_icon-balloon_buzz\\",\\"style\\":\\".vc_pixel_icon-balloon_buzz{--wpr-bg-fd609059-a4cd-49aa-bff3-96a375479f7d: url(\'https:\\\\/\\\\/ucp.edu.pk\\\\/wp-content\\\\/plugins\\\\/js\\n\\n[Truncated for database storage]", "wordCount": 139, "matchPages": 32, "matchWords": 15, "commonWords": 15, "uniqueWords": 124, "matchPercent": 11, "commonPercent": 11, "duplicateWords": 0, "duplicatePercent": 0}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/session-on-disaster-management-awareness-investigating-today-to-save-lives-tomorrow/", "text": "Session On Disaster Management Awareness: Investigating Today To Save Lives Tomorrow Home » News » Session On Disaster Management Awareness: Investigating Today To Save Lives Tomorrow UCP Disaster Management Society organized Session on Disaster Management Awareness: Investigating today to save lives tomorrow on 5th April, 2017. Mr. Mehr Ijaz Ahmed Achlana, Provincial Minister Disaster Management was Chief Guest of the ceremony. Mr. Rao Zaka ur Rehman, Manager Provincial Disaster Management Red Crescent Punjab and Mr. James Ulin, Regional Security Officer Lahore Pakistan were the Guest Speakers. The purpose of conducting this seminar was to create awareness regarding disasters and how to effectively manage them. Dr. Ayesha Azhar, Patron Disaster Management Society delivered the Welcome Note while Dr. Muhammad Zafarullah, Pro-Rector UCP delivered the vote of thanks. Session was culminated with Question Answer Session and presentation of Souvenirs. International Programs Merit List Apply Online Our Newsletter Facebook Twitter LinkedIn WhatsApp WhatsApp Us X", "title": "Session on Disaster M