 evaluation is important while comparing universities and choosing the one that suits you best, since you will be investing your money and a major part of your time. It is important to evaluate the rate of admission in the university and then how many actually leave after graduation, there would be many that would leave before even completing the university. Students withdrawal before graduation may not necessarily mean that the university is not good, you will have to make an effort to look into the reasons that why a number of students left. Do not reject a university on the basis of admission/graduation rate, no institute may be perfect, you just have to focus on the advantages that suit you. To get a deeper insight and clear your doubts you can visit the university and discuss in the admissions department. Finances Planning for the admission in university does bring some financial anxiety as it can be costly to attend one. Universities generally prefer rich students, but it doesn’t mean that less fortunate ones are neglected. If you feel that you need to be supported financially then it should be mentioned in your application. In case you meet the requirements then it’s all good but if by any means you think that you should be supported then you must mention it. This won’t hold anything against you in the admission process, but might be beneficial if you are really in need. Location Before taking admission you need to check where the university is located. If it is within the country then it is important to know the area so that you know the routes and distances. Also to make sure whether you would need live-in facilities or will be approaching from home. If you are taking admission in university of a foreign country, there are a number of things that you must consider, some of which are the weather of the country, type of food available, local language, interests of the people, social life, and how many people from your country prefer that place for study. If any of the before mentioned doesn’t suit you, then you would not be a very happy student since suitable living conditions matter. Quality of education/professors To best judge the quality of the education of a university you have to look into its graduate students, where they work and on what posts they are settled, keeping in mind that this cannot be judged by just a couple of students. Check the results of the university, how have the students been scoring? Do talk to students and take their views. Inquire about the environment of the university, and the professors. It is also very important to know how the professors are, specially the subjects they teach and how good they are at it. Learn about their teaching methodologies, the results they have been producing, and the number of students that turn over to them for guidance. Known courses for study Along with all the other important things it is very important to know the area in which the university excels, the subjects that it is known for. All universities may not be good in teaching all the subjects, for instance a medical college would not be able to teach computers and the university of law would be able to teach sciences. So know whether the university that you want to take admission in caters the subjects you require well or not. See where the students of the particular field are placed, get to know the professors and check the results of the subjects that you are interested in. Keep in mind that the university that you are applying in may be a good choice but not the right one for the subjects that you want to master. Extracurricular activities ‘A healthy body keeps a healthy mind’ is an old phrase but works well at every stage. Student life and on top of it being in a university, this is the prime time in the life of a human to learn all the good things and add them to their life so that they may excel not only in studies but in all the aspects of life. The university that you are opting for may be a very good choice but if it doesn’t support or have room for extra-curricular then know that you are about to become a book-worm. In your prospective university look for the magazine club, sports club, drama, volunteering. Taking part in extracurricular boosts up the energy to work and the knowledge about various subjects. If you are a writer and enjoy books, it’s a plus to have magazine club where you would be able to use your talent well. Sports are important for physical health, drama can open new doors of entertainment industry and volunteering helps rejuvenate the soul. Actively participating in other activities help to increase the confidence and believing in oneself. Also check whether the university is providing the Leadership opportunities or not. A university that instills the leadership qualities in its students help them go long way in life. Career services It is very important to know whether your prospective university provides career services or not. The major role of career services is to counsel and train the student for the upcoming professional life. At the university while completing your studies you can always turn to the career services office for proper guideline. There are many universities that arrange internships for their students later which can either convert to a full time paying job or can help acquire a job. See that the university you are planning for your admission has staff to guide the students for their professional choices. Safety Last but not the least, a secure environment counts the most. Check where your university is located, whether the location is safe or not. Note whether it has closed surroundings or not, check the building for proper safety measures that have been taken or not. See if the students are provide proper university identity cards and access to enter is solely on the identification of the student. The persons entering are gone through a proper security check and no trespassers are allowed. Do see how many entry access points are there. International Programs Merit List Apply Online Our Newsletter Facebook Twitter LinkedIn WhatsApp WhatsApp Us X", "title": "8 Things To Know Before Getting Admission In A University", "sizeKb": 169.8, "matches": [{"text": "International Programs Merit List Apply Online Our Newsletter Facebook Twitter LinkedIn WhatsApp WhatsApp Us X", "type": "common", "matchPages": [{"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/faculty-of-sciences/", "title": "Faculty of Sciences - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/seminar-on-general-awareness-of-traffic-laws/", "title": "Seminar on General Awareness of Traffic Law - UCP"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/skype-chat-session-with-the-head-of-school-massey-university-new-zealand/", "title": "Skype Chat Session with The Head of School, Massey University NZ"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/guest-lecture/", "title": "Guest Lecture - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/session-on-disaster-management-awareness-investigating-today-to-save-lives-tomorrow/", "title": "Session on Disaster Management Awareness: Investigating Today - UCP"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/psychology-society-seminar/", "title": "Psychology Society Seminar - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/news/levis-recruitment-drive-for-the-positions-of-store-managers/", "title": "Levi’s Recruitment Drive for The Positions of Store Managers - UCP"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/life-at-ucp-events/ramadan/", "title": "Ramadan - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/life-at-ucp-events/trophy-comes-home/", "title": "Trophy Comes Home - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/life-at-ucp-events/cultural-carnival/", "title": "Cultural Carnival - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/life-at-ucp-events/shab-e-midhat/", "title": "Shab-e-Midhat - University of Central Punjab"}, {"url": "https://ucp.edu.pk/life-at-ucp-event